.TH PGN-COUNT 1 "November 2026" "pgn-count" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pgn-count \- count chess games in PGN files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pgn-count
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR [\fIFILE ...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pgn-count
counts chess games in one or more Portable Game Notation (PGN) files. It
prints a count for each file and, when more than one file is given, their
combined total.
.PP
Use the file name
.B -
to read standard input alongside other files. At least one file name is
required, and standard input can be named only once.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -n , " " --no-filename
Do not print file names with per-file counts.
.TP
.BR -r , " " --results
Also show the number of white wins, black wins, draws, and undecided games.
The final result marker in the moves takes priority; if it is missing, the
\fBResult\fR tag is used. A game without a recognized result is counted as
undecided.
.TP
.B --strict
Stop after the first file that cannot be read or parsed. Without this option,
the program reports the error and continues with later files.
.TP
.BR -s , " " --summary
Print only the combined total.
.TP
.B --help
Show usage and options.
.TP
.B --version
Show the version number.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B pgn-count club.pgn
Count games in one file.
.TP
.B pgn-count --results games-a.pgn games-b.pgn
Count games and results in both files, then show their total.
.TP
.B cat games.pgn | pgn-count --summary
Print only the total number of games from standard input.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status is 0 when all requested inputs are counted, and 2 if an input
cannot be read or parsed or the command line is invalid.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pgn-list (1),
.BR pgn-reverse (1)
